00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.000
3.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.750
By the way, Adam's birthing pod in this scene
has some similarities to the cocoon we saw

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:18.979
with the Collector in the first Guardians
movie and which many people at the time thought

00:01:18.979 --> 00:01:21.510
could have been an Adam Warlock easter egg.

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:25.750
This time around though, the pod definitely
is a nod to the cocoon in which the gold-skinned

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:28.770
Adam Warlock was formed in the comics.

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:33.979
Warlock was created in Fantastic Four #66
by a group of scientists called the Enclave

00:01:33.979 --> 00:01:38.399
who sought to genetically engineer a perfect
race of human beings that could rule over

00:01:38.399 --> 00:01:39.399
the world.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:43.390
Initially, the character had no name, and
was only referred to as "Him", and I liked

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:48.869
the movie's subtle call-out to that fact when
Ayesha says, "I think I shall call him…

00:01:48.869 --> 00:01:49.869
Adam."

00:01:49.869 --> 00:01:53.210
Ayesha thinks she's created a powerful antagonist
to the Guardians of the Galaxy.

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:58.210
But I wonder if she might get a nasty surprise
when Adam finally emerges from his birthing

00:01:58.210 --> 00:02:03.299
pod, as in the comics, Adam's creators were
also going to manipulate him to do their bidding,

00:02:03.299 --> 00:02:07.829
but that did not end well for them as he didn't
like their nefarious plans and escaped pretty

00:02:07.829 --> 00:02:11.150
sharpish, leaving behind a scene of devastation.

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:14.849
On the other hand, it's possible that when
Adam appears properly in the next Guardians

00:02:14.849 --> 00:02:19.780
movie, he'll feel a kind of kinship or connection
with Ayesha because they've both been created

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:24.319
in birthing pods, and designed to be physically
and mentally impeccable, as all the Sovereign

00:02:24.319 --> 00:02:25.500
people are.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:29.909
By the way, in the comics, like Adam Warlock,
Ayesha was also created by the Enclave group

00:02:29.909 --> 00:02:32.180
of scientists and lashed out against them.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:36.890
Her comic-book backstory is rather complicated,
but suffice to say that in one of her early

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:41.310
forms, she was known as "Her", before taking
on the name of Kismet, and later Ayesha.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:46.379
OK, getting back to Adam Warlock: in the comics,
later he becomes a member of the Guardians

00:02:46.379 --> 00:02:47.379
of the Galaxy.

00:02:47.379 --> 00:02:50.890
However, in the MCU, at the moment, it looks
like he's being set up to work with Ayesha

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:54.780
as an antagonist to the Guardians, which is
intriguing because, in the comics, there's

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:57.989
an evil version of Adam Warlock known as the
Magus.

00:02:57.989 --> 00:03:02.831
The Magus is actually a god who is worshipped
by the Universal Church of Truth, and I think

00:03:02.831 --> 00:03:07.200
there's a really interesting link here with
the MCU's Ayesha, who is the High Priestess

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.420
of the Sovereign race.

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:14.069
So, could the Sovereign actually be the MCU's
own take on the Universal Church of Truth,

00:03:14.069 --> 00:03:18.730
the intolerant religious sect that went on
an expansionist rampage throughout the comic-book

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:19.730
universe?

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:23.500
And could the film's version of Ayesha play
a similar role to the Matriarch, who was the

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:25.239
leader of the Church in the comics?

00:03:25.239 --> 00:03:27.409
I'd love to know your thoughts on that.

00:03:27.409 --> 00:03:31.100
In the comics, the Guardians of the Galaxy
stood up against the Church, so perhaps this

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:34.550
could be a future storyline we'll see in Guardians
of the Galaxy Vol. 3.

00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:39.530
And I wonder whether there's also a potential
link to another cosmic dark force in the MCU?

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:43.990
That is, Dormammu and the Dark Dimension,
which was introduced in the Doctor Strange

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:44.990
movie.

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:47.170
It'll be fascinating to see if they connect
these up.

00:03:47.170 --> 00:03:51.391
Now, one of the major comic book storylines
that Adam Warlock is crucial to is the Infinity

00:03:51.391 --> 00:03:56.580
Gauntlet and, in particular, he has a very
strong connection to the Soul Gem in the comics.

00:03:56.580 --> 00:04:00.930
It's a complicated and lengthy story which
involves masses of Marvel's heroes, Warlock

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:05.030
included, joining forces against Thanos, but
one of the highlights is that Adam Warlock

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:09.489
not only wields the Gauntlet himself, but
he also puts together the Infinity Watch,

00:04:09.489 --> 00:04:13.650
which was basically, individuals who each
protected one of the Infinity Gems.

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:17.860
If you're thinking this means we'll get Adam
Warlock introducing the Soul Stone in or before

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:22.690
Avengers: Infinity War, this is sadly very
unlikely because James Gunn doesn't plan to

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:27.440
introduce the character until Guardians of
the Galaxy Vol. 3, which takes place after

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:28.830
the Infinity War movie.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:34.090
Gunn has said, though, that as Guardians Vol.
3 is happening after the culmination of Marvel's

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:39.060
Phase 3, the third Guardians movie will launch
both new and old Marvel characters into the

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:43.539
next ten years and beyond, and there are big
plans ahead for the character of Adam Warlock

00:04:43.539 --> 00:04:45.720
in the Marvel cosmic universe.

